; The two shapes the *set* bound catches and no per-head bound can. Both
; are errors, which is why this is a sibling of `example.sjon` rather than
; part of it: the schema-export round-trip feeds `example.sjon` to ajv and
; needs it clean.
;
;   cat examples/plugins/head-counts/plugin.sjon \
;       examples/plugins/head-counts/example-set-bounds.sjon | sjon validate - --no-project

; Two DIFFERENT resources. `buffer: at most 1` and `sampler: at most 1` are
; both satisfied, since there is one of each. `:max-children 1` is the only
; thing that refuses it.
(bgl-entry :binding 0
  (buffer  :type uniform)
  (sampler :type filtering))

; NO resource. Every per-head bound is a ceiling, so an empty child list
; satisfies all of them; writing `(head :name buffer :min 1)` instead would
; demand a *buffer* specifically, which is a different and wrong claim.
; `:min-children 1` is "at least one of these, whichever".
(bgl-entry :binding 1)

; Two of the SAME. This one breaches both levels at once, and the validator
; reports only the per-head diagnostic: it names the line to delete, and
; the set's claim is implied by it. That is the suppression rule.
(bgl-entry :binding 2
  (buffer :type uniform)
  (buffer :type storage))
